WEBVTT

00:02.585 --> 00:03.586
You...

00:05.130 --> 00:07.674
What do you think you're doing,
playing the decoy?

00:09.259 --> 00:10.927
That little chat with Natalia...

00:11.594 --> 00:13.430
It was about Sakuya, wasn't it?

00:14.931 --> 00:15.932
I see...

00:18.351 --> 00:19.936
Please forgive my harsh manner.

00:20.603 --> 00:24.024
It was the actions of a retainer
who is devoted to his mistress.

00:25.734 --> 00:26.776
The truth is...

00:27.610 --> 00:29.320
I am Princess Sherry's knight.

00:32.323 --> 00:34.200
<i>Even now, after her passing,</i>

00:34.284 --> 00:37.120
the pledge of loyalty
in my heart still remains.

00:38.121 --> 00:41.249
Loyalty that extends to Empress Sakuya.

00:41.332 --> 00:44.544
And now that you know that,
if all your actions are to protect her,

00:46.796 --> 00:48.465
then I will gladly work with you.

00:52.719 --> 00:55.972
VAUGHN DOMAIN, BIEI

00:58.933 --> 01:01.478
I did it... Jugo Sumeragi...

01:02.270 --> 01:03.438
I killed him.

01:03.521 --> 01:06.941
Jugo Sumeragi's death...
was not your fault.

01:07.484 --> 01:08.902
<i>Ash Phoenix.</i>

01:09.819 --> 01:12.739
<i>I thought I did
a thorough background check, but...</i>

01:14.157 --> 01:15.158
LAVENDER HOME

01:15.241 --> 01:17.577
<i>I should be able to learn more here.</i>

01:19.245 --> 01:21.289
<i>I have to ascertain the truth.</i>

01:22.540 --> 01:23.666
<i>I have to.</i>

01:29.255 --> 01:31.466
I, Sakuya Sumeragi,

01:31.549 --> 01:34.552
command you to tell me everything
about Ash Phoenix.

01:34.636 --> 01:36.846
Be sure not to leave out a single detail.

03:08.980 --> 03:10.023
HAKODATE TRAINING GROUNDS

03:10.106 --> 03:12.817
<i>Oda. Munemori.
You're up next. Begin mock battle.</i>

03:12.901 --> 03:13.902
<i>Yes, sir!</i>

03:14.360 --> 03:15.904
And Ash, fight as you wish.

03:16.362 --> 03:17.363
<i>Understood.</i>

03:19.741 --> 03:22.744
<i>I say we split up and flank him.
Sounds like a plan.</i>

03:22.827 --> 03:24.954
<i>Munemori!</i>

03:25.038 --> 03:27.081
<i>Don't worry. I wasn't hit.</i>

03:27.165 --> 03:29.125
The shots came from inside the forest.

03:29.209 --> 03:30.335
<i>We're closing in.</i>

03:30.418 --> 03:31.419
<i>Let's go.</i>

03:32.045 --> 03:33.922
<i>Wait, it's remote-controlled.</i>

03:34.005 --> 03:35.715
<i>Hey, this feel like a trap to you?</i>

03:37.884 --> 03:39.636
Oda, Munemori, you're out.

03:40.261 --> 03:42.639
<i>You must be aware of everything
going on around you.</i>

03:42.722 --> 03:45.725
<i>If this was a real battle,
you'd both probably be dead.</i>

03:47.060 --> 03:49.395
I'm next! Are you up for the challenge?

03:51.606 --> 03:54.025
<i>Of course. Just try to keep up.</i>

03:57.445 --> 03:59.989
Ash and his younger brother Nichol
lost their parents

04:00.073 --> 04:02.116
during the era of the Britannian Empire.

04:02.200 --> 04:05.161
Like many children during that time,
they were war orphans.

04:08.039 --> 04:10.041
<i>Ash was such a lively boy.</i>

04:10.124 --> 04:13.378
<i>He always acted like a big brother
to the younger children.</i>

04:14.170 --> 04:16.047
<i>Nichol, on the other hand,</i>

04:16.130 --> 04:18.466
<i>was unfortunately
born with rather poor health,</i>

04:18.549 --> 04:22.178
<i>though his smile always managed
to brighten everyone's day.</i>

04:23.429 --> 04:26.307
Three years later,
when the Vogue Scheme was enacted,

04:26.391 --> 04:29.435
the two of them were adopted
and taken in by Lord Lunebelg.

04:30.270 --> 04:31.479
What's the Vogue Scheme?

04:31.854 --> 04:35.275
It was a temporary solution
created for the war orphans.

04:35.358 --> 04:38.111
They were taken in
and raised by wealthy Britannians.

04:38.736 --> 04:40.655
That's how they ended up
with Lord Norland.

04:43.491 --> 04:45.451
Be sure to look after
each other, okay?

04:46.619 --> 04:48.538
No! Don't go!

04:48.621 --> 04:50.957
Come on, Ruby. You know they have to go.

04:51.040 --> 04:55.253
No! Ash, Nichol,
I don't wanna say goodbye!

04:56.045 --> 04:57.505
This isn't goodbye, okay?

04:58.965 --> 05:02.051
I'm sure that we're gonna
each other again. We're family.

05:02.593 --> 05:03.594
You promise?

05:04.721 --> 05:07.056
Yup!
And to prove it, I'll give you this.

05:10.143 --> 05:11.311
You promise you'll...

05:11.394 --> 05:13.104
Me too! I promise!

05:14.063 --> 05:15.064
Okay!

05:15.148 --> 05:16.399
That settles it.

05:19.861 --> 05:21.029
BRITANNIA
LUNEBELG MANOR

05:21.112 --> 05:22.280
<i>From what I have heard,</i>

05:23.031 --> 05:26.326
<i>their lives at the Lunebelg Manor
were anything but peaceful.</i>

05:26.409 --> 05:29.203
Just a little further, Nichol.

05:29.287 --> 05:30.538
Okay.

05:40.298 --> 05:42.342
Easy now. Are you okay?

05:42.884 --> 05:45.803
I do not have use
for those who are weak.

05:45.887 --> 05:48.639
The older one stays.
The younger one can be disposed of.

05:49.807 --> 05:53.436
No, wait! I'll be useful enough
for the both of us, I swear!

05:53.519 --> 05:56.481
Please, I'll do whatever you ask!
Just let us stay together!

05:56.564 --> 05:57.732
I'll do anything!

06:03.404 --> 06:04.447
I've got you now!

06:04.989 --> 06:07.283
It's over! I win!

06:09.619 --> 06:11.871
<i>Haruka's been hit! Battle over!</i>

06:12.789 --> 06:15.333
<i>Your attacks
are impulsive and far too inefficient.</i>

06:16.584 --> 06:19.587
<i>The slightest delay
can be deadly on the battlefield.</i>

06:20.213 --> 06:23.508
Be conscious of taking out the enemy
with as little movement as possible.

06:35.103 --> 06:38.189
Your movements
are far too inefficient.

06:38.272 --> 06:42.485
It only takes a single cut to a vital area
of the body to kill a person.

06:42.902 --> 06:45.321
You should take out your enemy
with minimal effort.

06:45.780 --> 06:47.323
We're done for today.

06:47.949 --> 06:50.618
Why do I have to be the one
doing the babysitting...

06:50.701 --> 06:51.786
Wait!
- Hmm?

06:53.079 --> 06:55.373
I... I can still fight!

06:57.500 --> 07:00.878
Look, I don't care if you're
Lord Norland's favorite or whatever.

07:00.962 --> 07:04.173
But only one of us will distinguish
himself on the battlefield...

07:04.257 --> 07:05.925
and that will be me, Arnold Renck!

07:06.008 --> 07:07.009
Huh?

07:11.305 --> 07:12.306
Unacceptable.

07:12.390 --> 07:15.059
His fighting style
is unbecoming of a knight.

07:15.143 --> 07:17.562
It lacks any trace of dignity.

07:17.645 --> 07:21.983
All that matters is that he's useful.
He's an instrument for murder.

07:26.154 --> 07:27.363
Again?

07:27.447 --> 07:28.448
I can't do this anymore--

07:28.531 --> 07:30.867
I think you misunderstand
the situation.

07:30.950 --> 07:33.327
You don't have any choice in the matter.

07:33.411 --> 07:35.496
There's only one acceptable response.

07:36.038 --> 07:37.957
You say, "Understood."

07:41.377 --> 07:44.172
<i>If you find the killing
becomes too hard for you,</i>

07:44.255 --> 07:46.007
<i>then kill your heart.</i>

07:47.216 --> 07:49.927
<i>Do that,
and you'll no longer feel anything.</i>

07:53.139 --> 07:55.725
<i>And so, one after another,</i>

07:55.808 --> 08:00.313
<i>Ash was forced to assassinate anyone
who Lord Lunebelg found inconvenient.</i>

08:01.063 --> 08:04.442
<i>It did not take long for him
to be recognized for his achievements,</i>

08:04.525 --> 08:07.111
<i>and Ash quickly rose
through the military ranks.</i>

08:09.447 --> 08:10.448
LUNEBELG DOMAIN, FURANO

08:10.531 --> 08:12.617
I'm so glad
I finally get to spend some time

08:12.700 --> 08:14.035
with you today, Big Brother.

08:14.118 --> 08:17.038
I have to kill my heart.
- I saw the doctor the other day.

08:17.121 --> 08:18.623
He told me that my strength is improv--

08:18.706 --> 08:21.042
I have to kill my heart.
I have to kill my heart.

08:21.125 --> 08:22.126
Big brother?

08:22.210 --> 08:23.461
I have to kill my heart.

08:24.962 --> 08:27.381
I have to kill my heart.
I have to kill my heart.

08:28.424 --> 08:29.884
I'm sorry, Ash.

08:29.967 --> 08:32.512
It's my fault you're suffering like this.

08:33.930 --> 08:35.681
I'm fine Nichol, really.

08:39.143 --> 08:40.937
A letter from Lord Norland.

08:48.110 --> 08:50.112
Who is it? Who's out there?

08:52.949 --> 08:53.950
Ruby...

08:54.450 --> 08:55.451
Ash, is that...

08:55.993 --> 08:57.245
really you?

08:57.328 --> 08:59.622
Damn it. I wanted to see you...

08:59.914 --> 09:01.123
but not like this.

09:06.379 --> 09:07.463
I'm sorry.

09:08.172 --> 09:11.300
But we have to do this to survive.

09:12.260 --> 09:13.302
Nichol...

09:13.928 --> 09:14.929
Why...

09:15.012 --> 09:17.974
Hey, did you hear a gunshot?
It came from the courtyard.

09:24.897 --> 09:26.190
NEO-BRITANNIA GOVERNMENT OFFICE
IMPERIAL PALACE

09:26.274 --> 09:28.526
You know that was quite
the mess you left behind.

09:28.609 --> 09:30.069
Wasn't easy cleaning it up.

09:30.152 --> 09:32.822
Guess you might say...
you "blew it."

09:36.450 --> 09:39.870
I received reports of incompetence
on your last mission.

09:39.954 --> 09:42.707
I ran into an old acquaintance,
and lost focus.

09:42.790 --> 09:44.750
No! It's not his fault!

09:44.834 --> 09:47.211
I was trying to help out,
but I just got in the way.

09:47.295 --> 09:50.881
If it wasn't for me,
he would have succeeded.

09:50.965 --> 09:52.133
It's all my fault!

09:52.758 --> 09:55.761
My brother is always looking out for me.

09:55.845 --> 09:58.097
Always pushing his mind and body.

09:58.180 --> 10:00.558
He's past his limit. And yet, still...

10:01.392 --> 10:04.478
If I... If I weren't here
holding him back, then--

10:07.982 --> 10:09.859
Your wish has been granted.

10:11.694 --> 10:13.654
Your presence is no longer required.

10:18.868 --> 10:21.120
That was a bit much,
don't you think?

10:21.203 --> 10:22.747
The boy was unnecessary.

10:23.748 --> 10:27.877
His existence served no use.
Kill... Kill... Kill... Kill...

10:27.960 --> 10:29.045
Kill!

10:31.213 --> 10:32.465
Let it go.

10:32.548 --> 10:35.051
You'll only increase the body count.
Kill... Kill...

10:35.760 --> 10:38.721
Kill... Kill... Kill...

10:38.804 --> 10:40.473
What will happen to Ash?

10:41.223 --> 10:42.516
I'll leave that to you.

10:43.434 --> 10:45.311
Kill...

10:54.445 --> 10:56.447
Huh? Well, look at that.

10:56.530 --> 10:58.658
Looks like I finally
have someone to talk to.

10:58.741 --> 11:00.368
<i>Hey there, young man.</i>

11:00.451 --> 11:04.038
<i>You must have stolen a pretty penny
to end up stuck in this place.</i>

11:06.916 --> 11:08.959
I'm Jugo Sumeragi by the way.

11:10.044 --> 11:11.253
Nice to meet you.

11:15.007 --> 11:16.008
NEO-BRITANNIA GOVERNMENT OFFICE
FRONT SHRINE

11:16.092 --> 11:17.843
How many times
do I have to tell you?

11:17.927 --> 11:21.138
Quit adding things to my workload
whenever you feel like it!

11:21.889 --> 11:25.393
Damn it, damn it, damn it!

11:26.477 --> 11:27.520
Pardon me.

11:29.855 --> 11:32.400
It would seem
you've angered her once again.

11:32.483 --> 11:33.484
I have.

11:33.567 --> 11:35.444
I know this might be
difficult for you,

11:35.528 --> 11:39.323
but you must strive to become like
Empress Sakuya's father, Governor Jugo.

11:39.824 --> 11:42.451
It's vital you keep acting
as the true empress,

11:42.535 --> 11:44.245
and not merely as a puppet.

11:44.328 --> 11:47.581
I believe doing so
will ultimately result in her protection.

11:48.290 --> 11:49.333
I know.

11:52.128 --> 11:55.172
Admiring flowers
in such a brutal workplace?

11:55.756 --> 11:57.341
What a delightful fetish you have.

11:57.925 --> 11:59.343
Was there something you needed?

11:59.427 --> 12:02.388
Do you have any insight
as to where young Ash might be?

12:02.471 --> 12:04.306
Why not look into it yourself?

12:05.015 --> 12:06.183
To be honest with you,

12:06.267 --> 12:09.103
the person I'm really after
is someone he's connected to.

12:09.895 --> 12:12.273
As I recall,
you and Ash happened to grow up

12:12.356 --> 12:15.192
in the very same orphanage
for a number of years.

12:15.276 --> 12:16.360
So what?

12:16.444 --> 12:18.279
I'd prefer it if things were easier,

12:18.362 --> 12:21.323
but I might have to employ
slightly rougher methods

12:21.407 --> 12:23.284
to get what I need.

12:26.746 --> 12:27.872
<i>Let me guess.</i>

12:27.955 --> 12:31.125
Japanese food
isn't really your cup of tea.

12:32.042 --> 12:33.294
Excuse me, guard!

12:33.377 --> 12:36.297
<i>This poor boy
hasn't eaten anything in ten days.</i>

12:36.380 --> 12:38.924
<i>It was kind of you to switch
to a Japanese menu for me,</i>

12:39.008 --> 12:41.552
<i>but maybe we should
switch back to Western food.</i>

12:41.635 --> 12:43.804
Understood. I'll speak with my supervisor.

12:44.263 --> 12:46.640
Thanks so much. I really appreciate it.

12:48.225 --> 12:51.729
<i>You know, you're not going to last long
on just one bowl of soup a day.</i>

12:51.812 --> 12:52.938
<i>I mean, look at me.</i>

12:53.439 --> 12:55.691
Even through all of this,
I've still got an appetite.

12:56.192 --> 12:58.194
And maybe it's due
to the lack of exercise,

12:58.277 --> 13:00.029
but I've even put on a few pounds.

13:00.112 --> 13:02.615
I was about your size
when I was a younger man.

13:02.698 --> 13:03.866
If my daughter saw me now,

13:03.949 --> 13:06.786
I bet she'd go on
about how I "used to look cool."

13:06.869 --> 13:09.205
Anyway,
is there anything you do love?

13:11.165 --> 13:12.249
Nicho--

13:15.878 --> 13:16.962
It's coffee.

13:17.505 --> 13:18.631
Excuse me!

13:18.714 --> 13:21.425
Could we get a cup of coffee
for the young man, please?

13:22.009 --> 13:25.137
SAPPORO SPECIAL DETENTION CENTER

13:27.473 --> 13:29.600
Your execution
has been confirmed.

13:30.142 --> 13:32.603
I'll be back to notify you
of the exact date.

13:34.355 --> 13:37.274
It can't be. I was told
there wouldn't be an execution.

13:38.067 --> 13:39.068
<i>Makes sense.</i>

13:39.151 --> 13:40.903
If I'm executed,

13:40.986 --> 13:43.906
little Callis will succeed me
and take his place on the throne.

13:44.448 --> 13:46.033
This is all Norland.

13:46.617 --> 13:49.203
He clearly intends to establish
his own puppet regime

13:49.286 --> 13:50.412
and rule from the shadows.

13:50.496 --> 13:53.791
It's not right. You do not deserve
to die in a place like this, sir.

13:54.500 --> 13:55.751
Thank you.

13:55.835 --> 13:59.255
Truly. But it isn't
as if they'll overturn the execution.

14:00.089 --> 14:02.049
My own death
isn't something that scares me.

14:03.008 --> 14:05.678
But the thought of never seeing
my precious daughter again,

14:05.761 --> 14:06.846
that hurts.

14:10.975 --> 14:13.686
I'm sorry... It's breaking my heart.

14:14.687 --> 14:17.606
<i>I understand how that feels.</i>
- Hmm?

14:19.316 --> 14:20.484
<i>I'm the same way.</i>

14:22.778 --> 14:24.071
Are you now?

14:24.947 --> 14:26.031
I suppose so.

14:27.283 --> 14:29.493
If it's all right, I'd like to know more,

14:29.910 --> 14:30.911
<i>about you.</i>

14:31.453 --> 14:32.663
Huh?

14:34.081 --> 14:37.960
So Ash obliged.
And began to tell him everything.

14:39.086 --> 14:40.504
<i>I understand.</i>

14:40.588 --> 14:43.215
<i>Without your brother,
you've lost your will to go on.</i>

14:43.299 --> 14:46.677
<i>Well, that said, what you need
is to find something else to love.</i>

14:47.761 --> 14:48.929
Something else to love?

14:49.597 --> 14:53.684
Right. And whatever it is,
it's the thing that'll give you strength.

14:54.852 --> 14:56.061
Is that possible?

14:56.854 --> 14:58.230
Does it exist?

14:59.648 --> 15:01.233
Yes, it does.

15:01.901 --> 15:03.569
And I'm sure you'll find it.

15:06.363 --> 15:08.198
<i>Hey... I'm curious.</i>

15:08.991 --> 15:11.201
<i>Is there anything that you actually hate?</i>

15:11.285 --> 15:12.411
<i>Hmm?</i>

15:12.828 --> 15:15.331
Anything I hate. Huh...

15:15.998 --> 15:19.293
Not much. Though I do have
a ranking of the things I love.

15:19.376 --> 15:21.921
My daughter Sakuya being first, of course.

15:22.004 --> 15:25.132
And last place... might just be Norland.

15:25.215 --> 15:27.259
Guess I shouldn't say
something like that out loud.

15:27.343 --> 15:29.762
They might move up my sentence.

15:31.138 --> 15:34.183
I wonder how differently things
would've turned out for the two of us,

15:34.266 --> 15:35.768
if you had been our father.

15:36.226 --> 15:38.228
<i>Well, it's never too late for that.</i>

15:38.312 --> 15:39.313
Huh?

15:39.396 --> 15:41.148
If you want to become my son,

15:41.231 --> 15:43.067
then all you have to do
is marry my daughter!

15:43.150 --> 15:45.903
No, wait, wait, wait, wait! No, hold on!

15:45.986 --> 15:47.446
<i>I take that back!</i>

15:47.529 --> 15:49.198
<i>Sakuya isn't marrying anyone!</i>

15:49.281 --> 15:50.324
<i>Not as long</i>

15:50.407 --> 15:52.242
<i>as I live and breathe, that is!</i>

15:52.326 --> 15:54.161
<i>Speaking of your daughter...</i>
Yes?

15:54.244 --> 15:55.371
<i>...would you say she's pretty?</i>

15:55.454 --> 15:57.039
<i>You really have to ask me that?</i>

15:57.122 --> 15:58.749
<i>She's my daughter, so of course she is!</i>

15:58.832 --> 16:00.626
<i>She's the most beautiful girl
you'll ever meet!</i>

16:00.709 --> 16:02.044
<i>Wait, why are you asking?</i>

16:02.127 --> 16:04.380
<i>Are you trying to go after my daughter?
Is that it?</i>

16:04.463 --> 16:05.965
<i>No, it's not like that.</i>

16:06.048 --> 16:07.257
<i>It's just...</i>
Understood.

16:07.341 --> 16:09.426
<i>...when you said as long as you're alive,
I thought...</i>

16:10.010 --> 16:11.220
Governor Jugo.

16:11.303 --> 16:14.765
I've just received the word.
Your execution will be held tomorrow.

16:15.265 --> 16:16.600
Wait. Already?

16:16.684 --> 16:19.603
A terrorist group led by Kensei Kuroto
has risen up,

16:19.687 --> 16:21.271
and is demanding your release.

16:21.355 --> 16:24.274
However, you're being blamed
for that uprising.

16:24.358 --> 16:26.151
<i>Now that he's flushed out the resistance,</i>

16:26.235 --> 16:29.363
<i>I suppose that Norland no longer
has any reason to keep me around.</i>

16:29.446 --> 16:32.282
You're the one who saved my wife
and daughter when you were governor.

16:32.366 --> 16:35.285
There's no way that I can just sit by
and watch you die.

16:36.078 --> 16:37.579
If I were to escape,

16:37.663 --> 16:40.624
it would only lead
to more friction with Neo-Britannia,

16:40.708 --> 16:43.836
and would worsen the ongoing
oppression of the Japanese people.

16:43.919 --> 16:45.462
<i>What about your daughter?</i>
- Hmm?

16:46.088 --> 16:47.506
If they kill you,

16:47.589 --> 16:49.675
Norland will use her
as political leverage.

16:49.758 --> 16:52.511
Let me help! I'll save you
and your daughter!

16:53.053 --> 16:54.096
<i>Trust me!</i>

16:57.266 --> 17:00.686
Then both our lives are in your hands.
I'm trusting you.

17:05.649 --> 17:06.817
I have to ask again.

17:07.901 --> 17:10.529
You really do promise
that you'll protect my daughter?

17:10.612 --> 17:12.948
I've never broken a promise,
I won't start now.

17:13.699 --> 17:16.618
They're keeping her under house arrest
in the government office.

17:16.702 --> 17:17.953
I'm counting on you.

17:19.121 --> 17:21.123
So this is Sakuya Sumeragi...

17:25.419 --> 17:27.337
I'll go ahead.
Understood.

17:29.548 --> 17:31.216
Lord Norland was indeed correct.

17:31.675 --> 17:34.928
He anticipated an escape attempt
the moment the execution was confirmed.

17:35.679 --> 17:38.640
Don't! We're too exposed.

17:38.724 --> 17:39.892
We need to keep moving.

17:39.975 --> 17:40.976
Right!

17:45.814 --> 17:47.357
Jugo Sumeragi!

17:47.441 --> 17:50.069
Lord Norland has issued orders
to shoot you on sight

17:50.152 --> 17:51.653
should you attempt to escape.

17:52.196 --> 17:53.238
Get up!

17:53.906 --> 17:56.742
No. I'll never make it
out of here like this.

17:56.825 --> 17:57.868
But you...

17:59.244 --> 18:00.621
You have to survive.

18:02.372 --> 18:03.832
Was this your plan all along?

18:03.916 --> 18:06.794
You said that you've never
broken a promise before.

18:06.877 --> 18:08.796
So keep the promise you made to me!

18:10.089 --> 18:11.090
Go, Ash!

18:11.799 --> 18:14.218
Keep your word and protect my daughter!

18:16.053 --> 18:17.888
Lock on to the second target.

18:18.597 --> 18:19.598
Fire.

18:24.394 --> 18:25.395
All right.

18:26.271 --> 18:27.481
It'll be fine.

18:29.942 --> 18:33.445
Were you really in such a hurry to die
that you couldn't wait for tomorrow?

18:33.904 --> 18:35.989
Sorry for ruining your plans.

18:36.740 --> 18:38.617
Lock onto the first target.

18:39.368 --> 18:40.369
Fire.

18:46.583 --> 18:47.584
Well now,

18:47.668 --> 18:49.920
aren't you a resilient noble.

18:50.838 --> 18:53.006
Not that it's doing me any good.

18:54.925 --> 18:57.136
At least grant me a quick death.

18:58.512 --> 18:59.680
As you wish.

19:06.019 --> 19:09.106
I believe the order
regarding the brat was to get rid of him.

19:09.982 --> 19:12.776
It would appear that my duty
has come to an end.

19:17.406 --> 19:18.657
What happened?

19:19.867 --> 19:21.034
And why?

19:24.079 --> 19:25.205
What now...

19:28.041 --> 19:32.504
That night, Governor Jugo sacrificed
his own life to save Ash.

19:34.506 --> 19:35.716
<i>It can't be...</i>

19:38.552 --> 19:40.220
That lightning sounded close.

19:40.929 --> 19:42.598
Ash!

19:43.640 --> 19:45.976
You'll catch your death out there!
Come inside.

19:49.021 --> 19:52.191
My fault. It's all my fault.

19:54.401 --> 19:56.528
It should've been me who died tonight.

19:57.529 --> 19:58.530
Ash...

20:07.039 --> 20:08.165
He's dead!

20:09.166 --> 20:11.418
Jugo Sumeragi is dead!

20:11.501 --> 20:13.253
<i>I killed him!</i>

20:16.548 --> 20:17.633
<i>What...</i>

20:18.592 --> 20:19.801
<i>What have I done...</i>

20:22.596 --> 20:24.223
<i>He loved his brother...</i>

20:25.515 --> 20:28.310
<i>and I just impersonated him.</i>

20:29.895 --> 20:31.438
<i>I manipulated Ash.</i>

20:41.365 --> 20:42.658
It's you!

20:46.620 --> 20:48.497
I, Sakuya Sumeragi, command you!

20:49.206 --> 20:51.708
Just as you'd protect
the most important person to you,

20:51.792 --> 20:53.752
you will protect me the same way!

21:02.261 --> 21:04.513
<i>I didn't even need
to use the Geass...</i>

21:05.931 --> 21:08.308
<i>Ash was already trying to protect me.</i>

21:10.978 --> 21:12.145
<i>I...</i>

21:12.229 --> 21:13.897
<i>I can't be Rozé anymore.</i>

21:14.982 --> 21:16.358
<i>It just isn't right.</i>

21:17.567 --> 21:21.154
<i>Tracking you down
and lying in wait worked out well.</i>

21:21.238 --> 21:22.447
<i>Oh, don't bother with that.</i>

21:23.156 --> 21:24.950
<i>Your Geass won't work through this.</i>

21:25.492 --> 21:27.119
<i>You know young lady,</i>

21:27.202 --> 21:30.622
<i>you were using your Geass
pretty recklessly about town.</i>

21:32.374 --> 21:33.500
<i>Because of that,</i>

21:33.583 --> 21:37.254
<i>all sorts of details leading back to you
became rather public.</i>

21:38.588 --> 21:40.173
<i>Now, you'll be coming with me,</i>

21:41.341 --> 21:42.676
<i>Sakuya Sumeragi.</i>

21:44.469 --> 21:46.430
LUXEMBOURG DOMAIN
NATALIA'S MANOR

21:48.307 --> 21:50.100
What is the meaning of this?

21:51.101 --> 21:52.602
Natalia Luxembourg,

21:52.686 --> 21:54.896
there have been reports
of you aiding terrorists.

21:54.980 --> 21:57.024
You are being detained
on the charge of treason.

21:57.899 --> 21:59.568
SEVEN SHINING STARS HAKODATE HIDEOUT

22:00.485 --> 22:02.070
They're firing missiles at us!

22:02.696 --> 22:04.406
Get me
our members' location data.

22:04.489 --> 22:05.615
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

22:08.493 --> 22:12.164
Ash Phoenix! Let's feast to our reunion!

22:12.247 --> 22:15.751
You're about to fall from grace.
So allow me to savor the moment!

22:15.834 --> 22:17.711
I'm loving the new you!

22:17.794 --> 22:21.715
The mods really smoothed out your edges!
I can't wait to see you in action!

22:27.929 --> 22:30.932
So, young lady,
shall we begin?
